rule size_to_ship v1
description "The size to ship: the first size on the customer's list that is in stock. The fold answers a value of the enum the first output has, and `unavailable`, a value of that enum, when the list is empty or nothing on it is in stock"

enum size = small | medium | large | unavailable
enum stock = in_stock | out_of_stock

elements choices
  wanted    : size
  available : bool

outputs
  shipped : size

table stock_of
policy unique
| available | -> state : stock |
| true      | in_stock         |
| false     | out_of_stock     |

fold state over choices
  in_stock     -> take_first wanted
  out_of_stock -> next
  empty        -> unavailable
  exhausted    -> held

sequence second_in_stock
| wanted | available |
| small  | false     |
| medium | true      |
| large  | true      |

sequence none_in_stock
| wanted | available |
| large  | false     |

sequence empty_list
| wanted | available |

examples
| choices         | -> shipped  |
| second_in_stock | medium      |
| none_in_stock   | unavailable |
| empty_list      | unavailable |
